#: ../../source/docs/common-geofencing-landing-page.rst:181
#: 79e6e2fdf9a14116a93619ea13fbac4b
msgid "Use for R/C Training"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-geofencing-landing-page.rst:183
#: 2301b80e7ea5405583c4f4eb29e80071
msgid "One of the main uses of geo-fencing is to teach yourself (or someone else) to fly radio controlled vehicles. When you have a properly configured geo-fence it is very hard to crash, and you can try manoeuvres that would normally be too likely to end in a crash, trusting the autopilot to 'bounce' the vehicle off the geo-fence before the flight ends in disaster."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-geofencing-landing-page.rst:190
#: d36400345c674db28228815da61fbac2
msgid "Geo-fencing can be combined with any flight mode. So for a raw beginner, you would combine it with one of the stabilised flight modes . Once the pilot has gained some confidence you could combine it with ACRO mode in Copter or MANUAL mode in Plane, which gives direct control of the vehicle and allows for the most interesting aerobatic manoeuvres."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-geofencing-landing-page.rst:197
#: 6c748e0f101c453d92f518c2f498dea0
msgid "MAVLink support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-geofencing-landing-page.rst:199
#: 1c915a770b544a859c4ed58e87254583
msgid "ArduPilot will report the fence status via the MAVLink GCS protocol. The key status packet is called FENCE_STATUS, and is defined in \"ardupilotmega.xml\". A typical FENCE_STATUS packet looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-geofencing-landing-page.rst:207
#: 6eb5dabc08c744e297bad03e3bb00ab8
msgid "The breach_status field is 0 if inside the fence, and 1 if outside. The breach_count is how many fence breaches you have had on this flight. The breach_type is the type of the last breach (see the FENCE_BREACH enum in ardupilotmega.xml). The breach_time is the time in milliseconds of the breach since APM was booted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-geofencing-landing-page.rst:213
#: c6e62181bbf4451dbb22eecd0e6d0be9
msgid "The MAV_SYS_STATUS_GEOFENCE bit of the MAV_SYS_STATUS_SENSOR portion of the SYS_STATUS message indicates whether or not the geo-fence is breached.  As of this writing only the MAVProxy GCS recognizes this status bit and reports the status of the geo-fence.  In the future the Mission Planner, APM Planner, and other GCS applications should get support for announcing geo-fence status during the flight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-geofencing-landing-page.rst:220
#: 9157a7be3b2740e3bdc9d6e76a75bd81
msgid "The MAV_CMD_DO_FENCE_ENABLE MAVLink command message allows a GCS to enable or disable a fence interactively.  As of this writing only MAVProxy supports this message using the \"fence enable\" or \"fence disable\" commands.  In the future Mission Planner, APM Planner, and other GCS applications may get support for interactively enabling and disabling the geo-fence without needing to use a manual transmitter."
msgstr ""
